The aim of this R tutorial is to familiarize you with how to perform Genome Wide Association Studies (GWAS) using a General Linear Model (GLM). ThE following packages also incorporates Principle Companent Analysis (PCA) to power the the GWAS analysis. 

The packages qqman and ggplot2 are needed to do GWAS analysis, 
After downloading packages, make sure to load them into R. 
For more details see the code below.

# Install qqman package (if not installed yet)

install.packages("qqman")
install.packages("bigstatsr")

```{r}
#Load functions
library(ggplot2)
library(qqman)
library(bigstatsr)
library(usethis)
library(devtools)

source("http://zzlab.net/StaGen/2020/R/G2P.R")
source("http://zzlab.net/StaGen/2020/R/GWASbyCor.R")
source("http://zzlab.net/GAPIT/gapit_functions.txt")

devtools::install_github("wcrump/GWASP")
library(GWASP)
```

